    "created_at": "2026-07-27T17:11:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-27T17:11:28Z",
    "body": "Here's another interesting test-case:\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<picture id=picture>\n  <source srcset=\"https://wpt.live/images/green.png?source\" media=\"(min-width: 800px)\"></source>\n  <img onload=\"console.log('load', this.complete)\" onerror=\"console.log('error', this.complete)\" src=\"https://wpt.live/images/green.png?src\" alt fetchpriority=\"high\">\n</picture>\n<div id=\"container\"></div>\n<script>\n  document.querySelector(\"img\").addEventListener(\"load\", function() {\n    let img = this;\n    let picture = document.getElementById(\"picture\");\n\n    console.log(\"before append\", img.complete);\n\n    container.appendChild(picture);\n\n    console.log(\"after append\", img.complete);\n\n    img.addEventListener(\"load\", () => console.log('once load', img.complete), { once: true });\n    img.addEventListener(\"error\", () => console.log('once load', img.complete), { once: true });\n  });\n</script>\n```\n\nWe react to environment changes and queue an image task. We report `complete=false` (because there's a queued image task) but `load` never arrives.\n\nThis is causing a compat issue in firefox (https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2058110). I think in this case we wouldn't need to trigger the load but if the image was inserted into a separate picture element we would and still it'd show the issue...\n\nThe spec doesn't account for the \"has a pending microtask\" at all.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
